  "label": "Body Dysmorphia",
  "description": "The meme implicitly references the psychological condition of body dysmorphia, where individuals have a distorted perception of their own appearance, often fixating on perceived flaws. The text 'when you are that ugly you don't have a choice' can be interpreted as reinforcing the idea that one's appearance dictates their life, which may exacerbate feelings of inadequacy or self-hatred associated with body dysmorphia. This is a real-world mental health concept that is not visible in the image but is necessary to understand the meme's potential psychological impact.",
